WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.466 --> 00:00:01.863
- I always said this for many, many years,

00:00:01.863 --> 00:00:03.783
the fans cannot fight for you.

00:00:03.783 --> 00:00:06.045
And one thing I know
I can do, I can fight.

00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:07.850
I'm a chess player, I play chess.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.028
Every move is calculated.

00:00:09.028 --> 00:00:12.400
I get my credit about
what I do in the ring,

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.118
but I don't get my credit
about what I do on the outside.

00:00:16.118 --> 00:00:17.672
- Hello Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:17.672 --> 00:00:20.601
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.325
more than they believe in themselves,

00:00:22.325 --> 00:00:25.316
and my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:28.686
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:28.686 --> 00:00:29.849
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:31.066
today we're going to learn from one of

00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:33.885
the greatest boxers of all
time, Floyd Mayweather,

00:00:33.885 --> 00:00:37.496
and my take on his top 10
rules of success, volume two.

00:00:37.496 --> 00:00:39.365
Rule number seven is my personal favorite,

00:00:39.365 --> 00:00:42.088
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:42.088 --> 00:00:43.848
Also, as you're watching,
if you hear something

00:00:43.848 --> 00:00:45.338
that really resonates with you,

00:00:45.338 --> 00:00:46.841
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:46.841 --> 00:00:48.250
and put quotes around
it so other people can

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:50.678
be inspired by it as
well, and if you leave it

00:00:50.678 --> 00:00:52.948
within the first couple hours
of this video going live,

00:00:52.948 --> 00:00:57.031
you have a chance to win
one of two daily prizes.

00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:01.424
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.742 --> 00:01:11.256
- You have to have a certain
charisma about yourself,

00:01:11.256 --> 00:01:14.324
a certain look about yourself.

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:16.836
That Pay-per-view attraction,
that Pay-per-view look.

00:01:16.836 --> 00:01:20.606
I know, because I was a young
kid and I had that same look.

00:01:20.606 --> 00:01:23.759
Certain fighters, Oscar De
La Hoya, he had that look,

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:25.406
Sugar Ray Leonard had the look,

00:01:25.406 --> 00:01:27.321
Mike Tyson had the look.

00:01:27.321 --> 00:01:29.191
Certain fighters have that
look and that charisma

00:01:29.191 --> 00:01:31.922
about them to become Pay-per-view stars.

00:01:31.922 --> 00:01:35.033
And if anybody know about who can become

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:37.138
a Pay-per-view star, you're talking to

00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:39.901
the king of Pay-per-view.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:44.183
You have to realize, we did so
many record breaking numbers,

00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:45.444
we don't no longer call it Pay-per-view,

00:01:45.444 --> 00:01:46.915
we call it May-per-view.

00:01:46.915 --> 00:01:50.066
- It reminds me of Ali and Frazier,

00:01:50.066 --> 00:01:52.443
not the fight, but the pregame.

00:01:52.443 --> 00:01:54.081
- [Floyd] The build-up, yes.

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:55.473
- The pregame.

00:01:55.473 --> 00:01:57.297
And I'm watching you, I know you,

00:01:57.297 --> 00:01:58.130
you're my friend.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.329
I'm watching you hold your composure.

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:03.087
It's a few times you
wanted to sock that mother.

00:02:03.087 --> 00:02:05.473
And I know you, and I know you
was being very professional

00:02:05.473 --> 00:02:10.214
saying I'm the boss, I must
conduct myself in a boss manner

00:02:10.214 --> 00:02:14.017
in front of my employee, 'cause
nigga you is my employee.

00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:16.878
Is that the attitude that you had?

00:02:16.878 --> 00:02:20.094
- I mean, I just felt like, you know,

00:02:20.094 --> 00:02:22.576
taking the chance of when he
touched me a couple times,

00:02:22.576 --> 00:02:23.409
when he said some--

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.320
- Hello.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.827
- Very disrespectful remarks a few times.

00:02:26.827 --> 00:02:30.040
He said a few things
that pushed my buttons,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.790
but just with experience
I'm not fixin' to...

00:02:35.957 --> 00:02:38.953
In the long run it'll cost
us hundreds of millions

00:02:38.953 --> 00:02:41.093
that we all could be
putting in our account

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.023
if we do it the smart way so I say,

00:02:43.023 --> 00:02:45.939
you know what, I'm a hold
out, wait 'til August 26th.

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:46.959
- [Snoop Dogg] Righteous.

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:48.552
- And do it when it counts.

00:02:48.552 --> 00:02:51.495
I'm not going to do it
when it don't count.

00:02:51.495 --> 00:02:55.734
I never focus on anything but
the guy that's in front of me

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.352
because when it comes down to it,

00:02:57.352 --> 00:02:58.945
I always said this for many, many years,

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.220
the fans cannot fight
for you and one thing

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.105
I know I can do, I can fight.

00:03:03.105 --> 00:03:06.188
So, the fans when they shout, scream,

00:03:08.101 --> 00:03:09.451
I don't worry about nothing.

00:03:09.451 --> 00:03:13.552
I just keep my composure
and stick to the game plan.

00:03:13.552 --> 00:03:15.585
Constantly keep coming
ahead, coming ahead.

00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:17.250
Pushing him, pushing him,

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.605
pushing him back, pushing him back.

00:03:20.605 --> 00:03:23.520
When he first come out for the
first 20 seconds of the round

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.393
when he go down, when
he go back to his corner

00:03:26.393 --> 00:03:28.569
and he sit down, I said when he come out,

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:30.716
he going to come out for
30 seconds and fight hard.

00:03:30.716 --> 00:03:33.161
And then he going to
break and once he break,

00:03:33.161 --> 00:03:34.627
that's when I'm going
to shoot the hard shot

00:03:34.627 --> 00:03:36.765
to the body, hit him
with a hard shot up top

00:03:36.765 --> 00:03:38.909
and keep pushing him back,
keep pushing him back.

00:03:38.909 --> 00:03:42.911
Remember, I told you guys
weight doesn't win fights.

00:03:42.911 --> 00:03:44.443
Fighting wins fights.

00:03:44.443 --> 00:03:48.188
And then when I said
talking doesn't win fights,

00:03:48.188 --> 00:03:50.094
fighting wins fights.

00:03:50.094 --> 00:03:54.261
Meaning that when we was on
the stage for the weigh in,

00:03:55.632 --> 00:03:57.608
I don't have to do no more talking.

00:03:57.608 --> 00:03:59.688
We fighting tomorrow
so I did enough talking

00:03:59.688 --> 00:04:01.795
on our tour, basically.

00:04:01.795 --> 00:04:03.565
So everybody said, oh, Mayweather,

00:04:03.565 --> 00:04:04.661
you was talking on the tour.

00:04:04.661 --> 00:04:06.773
Okay, I did a lot of talking on the tour,

00:04:06.773 --> 00:04:09.023
but now it's time to fight.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:13.506
We 24 hours away from the
biggest fight in the world.

00:04:13.506 --> 00:04:15.108
The biggest combat fight in the world.

00:04:15.108 --> 00:04:17.333
There's no need to talk anymore.

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:19.650
There's no need to talk anymore.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.233
It's a kid, a kid named Taylor.

00:04:24.074 --> 00:04:25.241
He has cancer.

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:29.803
Kid said, my only wish before I die

00:04:29.803 --> 00:04:31.940
is to meet Floyd Mayweather.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.273
And that's not the only kid

00:04:37.324 --> 00:04:39.459
that has said that that is his wish.

00:04:39.459 --> 00:04:41.540
His or her wish.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.571
But this little kid named Taylor,

00:04:44.571 --> 00:04:48.571
and he came to the boxing
gym and waited for me.

00:04:51.781 --> 00:04:55.031
I got here on time and when I seen him,

00:04:56.153 --> 00:05:00.239
it brought tears to my
eyes because he reminded me

00:05:00.239 --> 00:05:04.156
of my oldest son, when
my oldest son was young.

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:07.734
And this kid is only 10 years old.

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:11.067
So, we took a picture after he was here.

00:05:12.251 --> 00:05:14.007
He seen me box, he seen me train.

00:05:14.007 --> 00:05:17.424
We talked, he asked me so many questions.

00:05:19.444 --> 00:05:21.361
But, we took a picture.

00:05:25.459 --> 00:05:27.988
I wanted to post it on social media

00:05:27.988 --> 00:05:30.004
and I couldn't post it

00:05:30.004 --> 00:05:33.655
'cause I couldn't find the words to say.

00:05:33.655 --> 00:05:36.985
Every day I think about
this child, every day.

00:05:36.985 --> 00:05:38.703
So yesterday when I woke up,

00:05:38.703 --> 00:05:40.424
before I came to the boxing gym,

00:05:40.424 --> 00:05:42.265
I said, you know what I want to do today?

00:05:42.265 --> 00:05:43.098
I want to call Taylor.

00:05:43.098 --> 00:05:46.369
I want to spend time with this kid.

00:05:46.369 --> 00:05:49.036
So, I got in touch with his dad.

00:05:50.756 --> 00:05:53.759
I said, I want to go to GameStop.

00:05:53.759 --> 00:05:55.821
Went to GameStop, took the kid in there,

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:59.071
I said, get everything you want to get.

00:06:02.881 --> 00:06:05.964
Life if priceless, life is priceless.

00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:11.660
And your health is your wealth.

00:06:14.231 --> 00:06:17.064
So a lot of times, they say Floyd,

00:06:18.227 --> 00:06:19.295
won't you stick around boxing,

00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:22.288
you can make this and you can
make that, you can make this.

00:06:22.288 --> 00:06:26.288
Two years off, I could
have made a ton of money.

00:06:27.633 --> 00:06:29.867
But remember, your health is your wealth.

00:06:29.867 --> 00:06:31.780
- And to the fans that are still upset

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.278
with what went on in the
Pacquio fight, you say what?

00:06:34.278 --> 00:06:37.569
- The fans have to be mad at Pacquio.

00:06:37.569 --> 00:06:40.362
They can't be mad at me, I done my job.

00:06:40.362 --> 00:06:42.678
I never said I was a checkers player.

00:06:42.678 --> 00:06:44.200
I'm a chess player, I play chess.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.283
Every move is calculated.

00:06:47.919 --> 00:06:49.279
But the fans should
have thought about that

00:06:49.279 --> 00:06:53.446
when I was running through
everybody at one particular time.

00:06:54.343 --> 00:06:56.585
So now I'm just older and wiser.

00:06:56.585 --> 00:06:59.604
I'm older and wiser, it's like fine wine.

00:06:59.604 --> 00:07:01.127
I get better with time.

00:07:01.127 --> 00:07:05.294
Everybody know in this room
that's watched me fight,

00:07:06.453 --> 00:07:09.711
I could've easily
out-boxed Conor McGregor,

00:07:09.711 --> 00:07:12.210
counter-punched him all night.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.304
That's not what I wanted to do.

00:07:14.304 --> 00:07:15.893
I wanted to go out with a bang.

00:07:15.893 --> 00:07:17.875
I told you guys I would
come straight ahead.

00:07:17.875 --> 00:07:22.055
I feel like I owed that to the
fans for the Pacquio fight.

00:07:22.055 --> 00:07:24.426
Even though I don't owe anybody nothing,

00:07:24.426 --> 00:07:27.573
I put the pressure on
myself and did it myself,

00:07:27.573 --> 00:07:28.406
and that was a goal of mine.

00:07:28.406 --> 00:07:31.570
I told you guys that this
fight wouldn't go the distance.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.286
- It's over 300, not 200 million.

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:34.119
It's over 300 million dollars for tonight.

00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:34.952
- Yes.

00:07:34.952 --> 00:07:35.785
- 350.

00:07:35.785 --> 00:07:37.346
- 350, about 350 million.

00:07:37.346 --> 00:07:38.179
- So I broke my record.

00:07:38.179 --> 00:07:39.012
- So you broke your record.

00:07:39.012 --> 00:07:41.025
- I want to say this,
with ShowTime and CBS,

00:07:41.025 --> 00:07:41.858
with the deal they gave me,

00:07:41.858 --> 00:07:42.691
(mumbles)

00:07:42.691 --> 00:07:46.845
Three fights with the Canelo, the Pacquio,

00:07:46.845 --> 00:07:49.380
and this fight with Conor McGregor,

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.380
I think 750.

00:07:53.318 --> 00:07:54.612
I've made over a billion
dollars in my career,

00:07:54.612 --> 00:07:56.268
but just those three fights, 750.

00:07:56.268 --> 00:07:57.855
From CBS and ShowTime.

00:07:57.855 --> 00:08:00.188
- So, but your name is money

00:08:01.042 --> 00:08:02.347
and obviously that validates it.

00:08:02.347 --> 00:08:03.180
Are you sure--

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:04.013
- I'm through.

00:08:04.013 --> 00:08:05.718
- That if somebody else can't
come with a nine figure.

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:06.611
- Stop, just stop. No, stop.

00:08:06.611 --> 00:08:08.839
- I'm just asking, another nine figure?

00:08:08.839 --> 00:08:12.105
- Can you let me retire
and be happy, please?

00:08:12.105 --> 00:08:13.391
- I've tried three times.

00:08:13.391 --> 00:08:15.042
- Just please, please.

00:08:15.042 --> 00:08:17.147
- Okay, okay you're done, you're done.

00:08:17.147 --> 00:08:18.094
I'm not going to bother it again.

00:08:18.094 --> 00:08:18.927
- Tell them, tell them.

00:08:18.927 --> 00:08:20.846
- He's done, he's done
ladies and, he's done.

00:08:20.846 --> 00:08:22.849
It's over, it's over,
he's not fighting again.

00:08:22.849 --> 00:08:24.501
- You don't want nobody from MMA or boxing

00:08:24.501 --> 00:08:25.595
calling me out no more, tell them.

00:08:25.595 --> 00:08:27.269
- Don't call him out
anymore, he's retired.

00:08:27.269 --> 00:08:28.102
- Thank you.

00:08:28.102 --> 00:08:29.166
- He's retired, going to be happy.

00:08:29.166 --> 00:08:32.669
- A man that has never
been in the boxing ring

00:08:32.669 --> 00:08:35.448
is in the ring with the best ever,

00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:37.784
that's what you describe
yourself as being.

00:08:37.784 --> 00:08:39.799
- I don't describe myself.

00:08:39.799 --> 00:08:43.658
We must realize, men lie,
women lie, numbers don't lie,

00:08:43.658 --> 00:08:44.491
- 49-0.

00:08:44.491 --> 00:08:45.634
- Not just 49-0.

00:08:45.634 --> 00:08:47.244
- We've got time, I'm
listening, I'm listening.

00:08:47.244 --> 00:08:50.307
- Mayweather that's done
broke every record in boxing.

00:08:50.307 --> 00:08:51.923
When we get to talk about highest gate,

00:08:51.923 --> 00:08:55.460
even when they said Mayweather's
fight didn't sell out.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:58.921
Well, you know, when it do sell out,

00:08:58.921 --> 00:09:00.518
I think I reached somewhere like,

00:09:00.518 --> 00:09:02.957
the live gate it reached

00:09:02.957 --> 00:09:04.650
like 80-something million for this fight.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.089
Already, we already at
60-something million,

00:09:07.089 --> 00:09:08.940
for those they saying that Mayweather

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.357
is not doing numbers anymore.

00:09:14.489 --> 00:09:16.279
Far as taking the less punishment,

00:09:16.279 --> 00:09:19.676
I took less punishment than any fighter.

00:09:19.676 --> 00:09:23.292
Not just best defense,
let's talk about offense.

00:09:23.292 --> 00:09:26.459
The most accurate fighter of all time.

00:09:27.689 --> 00:09:29.258
On the outside the ring,
it's not just about

00:09:29.258 --> 00:09:30.878
being on the inside of the ring.

00:09:30.878 --> 00:09:32.913
I already conquered that.

00:09:32.913 --> 00:09:35.580
I'm even smarter on the outside.

00:09:38.719 --> 00:09:42.801
I have to be a genius to even
make a fight like this happen.

00:09:42.801 --> 00:09:45.461
So what does that say about me
for making this fight happen?

00:09:45.461 --> 00:09:48.606
- It says that you're a
brilliant business man,

00:09:48.606 --> 00:09:49.750
not just a great boxer.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.633
- And that's what I always spoke about,

00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:53.816
that's what I always spoke about.

00:09:53.816 --> 00:09:56.397
I get my credit about
what I do in the ring,

00:09:56.397 --> 00:10:00.892
but I don't get my credit
about what I do on the outside.

00:10:00.892 --> 00:10:02.572
- Where did you get that business sense,

00:10:02.572 --> 00:10:06.451
because you've surpassed
everybody in boxing,

00:10:06.451 --> 00:10:08.391
in sports, in everything in general.

00:10:08.391 --> 00:10:09.855
I'm watching you, it's like

00:10:09.855 --> 00:10:11.859
you bigger than the NFL franchise.

00:10:11.859 --> 00:10:14.276
- Just my team, me believing.

00:10:16.408 --> 00:10:18.075
I'm going to be honest,

00:10:20.825 --> 00:10:22.550
I have a team also,

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:24.209
but my team don't get in there

00:10:24.209 --> 00:10:26.541
and go to war like I go to war,

00:10:26.541 --> 00:10:28.018
but they go to war on the outside.

00:10:28.018 --> 00:10:29.986
My team go to war.

00:10:29.986 --> 00:10:32.653
I'm very, very tough on my team.

00:10:34.446 --> 00:10:36.863
I want my team to be the best

00:10:37.968 --> 00:10:39.902
that they can be on the outside.

00:10:39.902 --> 00:10:43.805
But as far as on the
outside, you know Al Haymon--

00:10:43.805 --> 00:10:44.826
- That's the OG right there.

00:10:44.826 --> 00:10:46.057
- That's OG, a legend.

00:10:46.057 --> 00:10:47.323
A legend.

00:10:47.323 --> 00:10:48.944
A very shrewd businessman.

00:10:48.944 --> 00:10:53.278
Leonard Ellerbe, Master's
degree in business.

00:10:53.278 --> 00:10:55.066
So, you know when you surround yourself

00:10:55.066 --> 00:10:55.899
with people like this,

00:10:55.899 --> 00:10:59.728
just being around certain individuals.

00:10:59.728 --> 00:11:02.955
Like, even being around Don
King, being around Bob Arum,

00:11:02.955 --> 00:11:04.817
being around just different
people that's been

00:11:04.817 --> 00:11:05.708
in the game a long time

00:11:05.708 --> 00:11:08.657
and you know, by being their buddies.

00:11:08.657 --> 00:11:10.623
You know, every time I got
around by being their buddies

00:11:10.623 --> 00:11:14.147
I was more like, it's cool
to come over to your house

00:11:14.147 --> 00:11:16.183
but I need a house like this.

00:11:16.183 --> 00:11:17.523
It's cool to ride on your yacht,

00:11:17.523 --> 00:11:18.697
but I need a yacht like this.

00:11:18.697 --> 00:11:19.530
It's cool to ride on your jet,

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.219
but I want a jet like this.

00:11:21.219 --> 00:11:23.968
And I said, no, I don't
want to ride on yours.

00:11:23.968 --> 00:11:25.137
You show me how to get it.

00:11:25.137 --> 00:11:28.028
You can't be my friend if you
can't show me how to get it,

00:11:28.028 --> 00:11:29.356
'cause once they show me how to get it,

00:11:29.356 --> 00:11:31.560
then I can install it in my children,

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.021
then it goes, it trickles down.

00:11:33.021 --> 00:11:35.155
- Bloodline, it's a bloodline thing.

00:11:35.155 --> 00:11:36.821
- Yes, so it's about wealth.

00:11:36.821 --> 00:11:38.819
You know, I'm no longer rich, I'm wealthy.

00:11:38.819 --> 00:11:41.026
Last thing about my career.

00:11:41.026 --> 00:11:44.190
I never want, as far as making weight,

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:48.357
when you asked me about
Cervantes tanked making weight.

00:11:49.218 --> 00:11:51.968
He's young, but when I was young,

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.294
I think I would have
made those same mistakes

00:11:56.294 --> 00:11:58.706
if I didn't have my father in my life.

00:11:58.706 --> 00:12:01.748
You know, just being a coach that

00:12:01.748 --> 00:12:04.307
was extremely hard on me.

00:12:04.307 --> 00:12:07.348
I think that if he didn't
discipline me in boxing,

00:12:07.348 --> 00:12:11.811
I don't even know how my
career would have played out.

00:12:11.811 --> 00:12:13.483
I didn't want to slack, and I didn't want

00:12:13.483 --> 00:12:16.557
to seem irresponsible or not disciplined,

00:12:16.557 --> 00:12:18.814
so that's why I always sacrificed.

00:12:18.814 --> 00:12:20.509
You got to sacrifice
something to get something.

00:12:20.509 --> 00:12:23.753
So that's why I've always made sacrifices

00:12:23.753 --> 00:12:26.547
to get to a certain level
and to get to the pinnacle,

00:12:26.547 --> 00:12:29.337
you got to make sacrifices
and that's what I did.

00:12:29.337 --> 00:12:31.746
- Why is the money so important?

00:12:31.746 --> 00:12:33.474
Why do you always come
back to the dollars?

00:12:33.474 --> 00:12:35.370
People want to know, I mean,

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.996
you obviously have a
fascination, you've earned a lot.

00:12:37.996 --> 00:12:40.891
You show it all the time,
you talk about it a lot.

00:12:40.891 --> 00:12:43.641
Why does it always come to money?

00:12:44.839 --> 00:12:45.672
- Why not?

00:12:47.053 --> 00:12:49.327
I mean everything you got on costs money.

00:12:49.327 --> 00:12:51.621
Everything you do costs money.

00:12:51.621 --> 00:12:54.017
You can't take your
wife on a date for free.

00:12:54.017 --> 00:12:56.182
- Is that how you measure your success?

00:12:56.182 --> 00:12:57.730
- No.

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:00.224
Me, I'm loyal and honest.

00:13:00.224 --> 00:13:03.462
And I'm a good person, and
I call a spade a spade.

00:13:03.462 --> 00:13:06.357
Money don't make me, I make money.

00:13:06.357 --> 00:13:08.529
And without money, I'd be the same person.

00:13:08.529 --> 00:13:10.946
I've so many fights for free.

00:13:12.577 --> 00:13:13.625
- You're getting emotional now.

00:13:13.625 --> 00:13:15.567
- No, not at all.

00:13:15.567 --> 00:13:17.294
No, I'm thinking.

00:13:17.294 --> 00:13:19.498
You know I'm always thinking.

00:13:19.498 --> 00:13:22.594
how can I get better,
how can our company grow,

00:13:22.594 --> 00:13:25.460
how can I continue to teach
people around me how to fish

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:28.550
and I don't want to fish for them.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:30.938
We teach you how to become entrepreneurs.

00:13:30.938 --> 00:13:32.972
And if we can't, we want you to be

00:13:32.972 --> 00:13:37.139
the best that you can be
if you're under the banner.

00:13:47.267 --> 00:13:50.241
(lighthearted music)

00:13:50.241 --> 00:13:52.309
Great dance partner to dance with.

00:13:52.309 --> 00:13:53.966
Conor McGregor, you a hell of a champion

00:13:53.966 --> 00:13:57.966
and to the country of
Ireland, we love you guys.

00:14:09.372 --> 00:14:11.622
(applause)

00:14:17.933 --> 00:14:20.442
- Big round of applause for
two classy, classy gentlemen.

00:14:20.442 --> 00:14:22.692
(applause)

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.037
- But I give him a hat's off,

00:14:34.037 --> 00:14:34.870
Fair play to him.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:35.895
He's a composed man.

00:14:35.895 --> 00:14:37.671
You can give him no more respect.

00:14:37.671 --> 00:14:41.089
He took the shots early,
and he took shots early.

00:14:41.089 --> 00:14:41.922
He cracked them with the left hand

00:14:41.922 --> 00:14:44.504
and I saw him in a bit
of panic but he stayed

00:14:44.504 --> 00:14:46.551
very very clam, that's just
his years of experience.

00:14:46.551 --> 00:14:49.312
- He's a tough competitor
and he still have

00:14:49.312 --> 00:14:50.916
a long career ahead of him.

00:14:50.916 --> 00:14:54.412
- Does he have a career in boxing?

00:14:54.412 --> 00:14:57.284
- We got to get his conditioning
a little bit better.

00:14:57.284 --> 00:14:59.420
- On that a little bit,
and explain what you liked

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.419
about the boxing business
and what you prefer

00:15:01.419 --> 00:15:03.336
about the MMA business.

00:15:07.586 --> 00:15:09.717
- The check is alright.

00:15:09.717 --> 00:15:10.595
The check is not bad.

00:15:10.595 --> 00:15:12.533
(laughs)

00:15:12.533 --> 00:15:14.089
Very good, but look...

00:15:14.089 --> 00:15:16.339
(mumbling)

00:15:17.663 --> 00:15:18.496
Great job.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:23.086
- Floyd, congratulations, terrific career.

00:15:23.086 --> 00:15:23.919
- Great work.

00:15:23.919 --> 00:15:26.972
- Good job, thank you, good job.

00:15:26.972 --> 00:15:29.933
- Ladies and gentlemen, to the podium,

00:15:29.933 --> 00:15:34.100
I'd like to call up The
Notorious One, Conor McGregor.

00:15:35.197 --> 00:15:37.447
(applause)

00:15:48.221 --> 00:15:49.346
- What's up everybody?

00:15:49.346 --> 00:15:50.791
He had to change his style of fair play.

00:15:50.791 --> 00:15:52.271
And he did, he adjusted,
he changed his style.

00:15:52.271 --> 00:15:54.194
He put the hands up, more forward.

00:15:54.194 --> 00:15:55.163
He's composed.

00:15:55.163 --> 00:15:57.243
He's not that fast,
he's not that powerful,

00:15:57.243 --> 00:15:58.426
but boy is he composed.

00:15:58.426 --> 00:16:00.955
Hands up toward your forehead, dipped in,

00:16:00.955 --> 00:16:02.906
forehead on the chest and decided

00:16:02.906 --> 00:16:04.503
to fight that kind of fight.

00:16:04.503 --> 00:16:07.361
I didn't anticipate that, three
game changes in the fight.

00:16:07.361 --> 00:16:09.461
That's what a true champion does.

00:16:09.461 --> 00:16:12.401
Much respect, you came with it.

00:16:12.401 --> 00:16:13.262
You know what I mean?

00:16:13.262 --> 00:16:14.095
I got to give respect to that.

00:16:14.095 --> 00:16:15.863
(applause)

00:16:15.863 --> 00:16:16.809
It was a hell of a fight.

00:16:16.809 --> 00:16:19.462
- Was he better than you had expected?

00:16:19.462 --> 00:16:21.201
- He's a lot better than I thought he was.

00:16:21.201 --> 00:16:23.791
He used different angles,
he was a tough competitor.

00:16:23.791 --> 00:16:26.427
But I was the better man tonight.

00:16:26.427 --> 00:16:29.201
- He was making me throw when
he was patient with his shots.

00:16:29.201 --> 00:16:31.295
I got to give him nothing
but respect though.

00:16:31.295 --> 00:16:34.462
Fair play, great career that he's had.

00:16:35.846 --> 00:16:37.087
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:37.087 --> 00:16:38.347
I made this video because

00:16:38.347 --> 00:16:40.733
DreamChasers Motivation asked me to.

00:16:40.733 --> 00:16:41.743
If there's someone
you'd like me to profile

00:16:41.743 --> 00:16:43.841
in our future top 10, please check out

00:16:43.841 --> 00:16:45.636
the link down in the description below

00:16:45.636 --> 00:16:48.988
and you can cast your vote
on who we should do next.

00:16:48.988 --> 00:16:50.894
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Cyrus Webb.

00:16:50.894 --> 00:16:52.627
Cyrus thank you do much for picking up

00:16:52.627 --> 00:16:54.600
a copy of my book Your
One Word and posting

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.930
that awesome picture to
your audience on Twitter,

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:59.174
and also the five-star
review you left on Amazon.

00:16:59.174 --> 00:17:01.660
I really, really, really
appreciate the support, man,

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.398
and I'm so glad you enjoyed the book.

00:17:03.398 --> 00:17:04.507
Thank you guys again for watching,

00:17:04.507 --> 00:17:05.867
I believe in you.

00:17:05.867 --> 00:17:07.736
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:17:07.736 --> 00:17:11.021
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:17:11.021 --> 00:17:12.521
I'll see you soon.

00:17:18.354 --> 00:17:19.470
- [Man] Floyd, just a follow up on Conor,

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.376
there's a lot of concern
coming into this fight

00:17:21.376 --> 00:17:22.880
that the rules were going to be followed,

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:24.100
and it was a little bit
rough at times in there,

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.744
there were some warnings.

00:17:25.744 --> 00:17:27.390
How did you feel about the way

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:31.332
Conor conducted himself
in the ring tonight?

00:17:31.332 --> 00:17:33.038
- I let the referee do his job.

00:17:33.038 --> 00:17:36.288
You know, I let the referee do his job.

00:17:37.222 --> 00:17:39.671
I'm not here to bash the referee,

00:17:39.671 --> 00:17:42.527
but you guys know what was going on.

00:17:42.527 --> 00:17:45.562
A lot of rapid punching, a lot.

00:17:45.562 --> 00:17:48.979
Things happen but you live and you learn.

00:17:51.113 --> 00:17:52.632
The referee is a hell of a referee,

00:17:52.632 --> 00:17:54.104
Conor McGregor is a hell of a fighter.

00:17:54.104 --> 00:17:55.465
I'm not here to bash anyone.

00:17:55.465 --> 00:17:56.458
I just went out there
to do my job tonight.

00:17:56.458 --> 00:17:58.701
- As you've been away from the game

00:17:58.701 --> 00:18:00.999
and you reflect on your life
and your career right now.

00:18:00.999 --> 00:18:01.832
- Yes.

00:18:03.652 --> 00:18:04.985
- Where are you?

00:18:06.888 --> 00:18:08.738
Just looking at the life
of Floyd Mayweather.

00:18:08.738 --> 00:18:10.664
- Just looking at my life?

00:18:10.664 --> 00:18:14.831
I don't think most people
could handle being in my shoes.

00:18:16.864 --> 00:18:17.697
Yo, yo.

00:18:20.107 --> 00:18:22.107
- You good, you're good.

00:18:23.455 --> 00:18:26.624
- I mean, as of right now I don't think.

00:18:26.624 --> 00:18:28.828
no one could handle my situation.

00:18:28.828 --> 00:18:29.955
- [Interviewer] Why not?

00:18:29.955 --> 00:18:31.164
- They just can't.

00:18:31.164 --> 00:18:32.948
- [Interviewer] What's your
situation that can't be handled?

00:18:32.948 --> 00:18:36.073
- I'm saying, they feel
like it's pressure on me.

00:18:36.073 --> 00:18:40.568
Like I said, they tried to
defeat me in many different ways.

00:18:40.568 --> 00:18:43.083
They try to bring up the tax thing,

00:18:43.083 --> 00:18:46.072
they try to bring up he's been locked up,

00:18:46.072 --> 00:18:47.410
he's arrogant, he's unappreciative.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:50.198
I mean, years and years and
years they've been trying

00:18:50.198 --> 00:18:53.031
their best to defeat me, mentally.

00:18:56.247 --> 00:18:57.539
I can't be defeated.

00:18:57.539 --> 00:18:58.834
I'm a strong individual.

00:18:58.834 --> 00:19:00.878
Nothing can throw me off.

00:19:00.878 --> 00:19:03.807
Nothing can throw me off key.

00:19:03.807 --> 00:19:07.573
I'm always focused on what I got to do.

00:19:07.573 --> 00:19:09.209
- And that's going to
be the case August 26th?

00:19:09.209 --> 00:19:12.015
- August 26th going to
be real interesting.

00:19:12.015 --> 00:19:13.749
And I'm not backing up.

00:19:13.749 --> 00:19:15.042
Remember I told you that.

00:19:15.042 --> 00:19:16.045
- [Interviewer] You're not backing up?

00:19:16.045 --> 00:19:16.923
- I'm not backing up.

00:19:16.923 --> 00:19:20.423
I hustled a hustler, I go for the jugular.

00:19:21.518 --> 00:19:24.063
Couldn't work not job, I
probably cuss out the customer.

00:19:24.063 --> 00:19:26.303
(laughter)

00:19:26.303 --> 00:19:28.629
I'll smuggle the smuggler,

00:19:28.629 --> 00:19:31.114
I'm the first from the grind.

00:19:31.114 --> 00:19:35.168
I'm a bad boy, always knew I would shine.

00:19:35.168 --> 00:19:39.219
I bang with the bangers,
I flame with the flamers.

00:19:39.219 --> 00:19:43.983
You know what my name is,
I'm more famous than Amos.

00:19:43.983 --> 00:19:48.063
I hate all the haters, cut
the lights off in Vegas.

00:19:48.063 --> 00:19:52.980
We making this money, but
this money don't make us.

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:55.939
I'm taking my time, ain't
got time for the taking.

00:19:55.939 --> 00:20:00.106
I went ham in the streets
just to bring home the bacon.

